WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.167 --> 00:00:02.335
-Welcome, everybody.
Welcome, welcome.

00:00:02.335 --> 00:00:03.502
I love you, too.

00:00:03.502 --> 00:00:05.137
Welcome to "The Tonight Show,"
everybody.

00:00:05.137 --> 00:00:10.410
[ Cheers and applause ]
Yeah!

00:00:10.410 --> 00:00:12.578
Well, guys,
after weeks of waiting,

00:00:12.578 --> 00:00:15.214
tomorrow afternoon,
at 1:15 p.m.,

00:00:15.214 --> 00:00:16.849
President Biden will hold
his first

00:00:16.849 --> 00:00:19.652
presidential press conference.

00:00:19.652 --> 00:00:21.787
People who normally watch soaps
will be like,

00:00:21.787 --> 00:00:24.457
"Who's the new beefcake
on 'Young &amp; The Restless'?"

00:00:24.457 --> 00:00:26.158
[ Laughter ]

00:00:26.158 --> 00:00:28.995
Yep, news ratings are down,
so CNN asked Biden

00:00:28.995 --> 00:00:30.563
if he'd be willing
to do the press conference

00:00:30.563 --> 00:00:32.031
dressed like
one of the Avengers.

00:00:32.031 --> 00:00:33.265
[ Laughter ]

00:00:33.265 --> 00:00:34.967
After being first
for four years,

00:00:34.967 --> 00:00:38.037
I wonder how many people Biden
will call on before Fox News?

00:00:38.037 --> 00:00:39.872
Be like,
"Yes, you in the back

00:00:39.872 --> 00:00:42.442
from the Sister Ignatius
Middle School Gazette."

00:00:42.442 --> 00:00:45.812
[ Laughter ]

00:00:45.812 --> 00:00:47.646
Biden's dealing with
North Korea,

00:00:47.646 --> 00:00:50.383
a border crisis,
and a global pandemic.

00:00:50.383 --> 00:00:52.218
But, of course,
the first question will be,

00:00:52.218 --> 00:00:54.320
"Sir, why did you fall
three times going up the stairs

00:00:54.320 --> 00:00:56.622
of Air Force One?
Follow up question!

00:00:56.622 --> 00:00:59.125
Is Major the Dog happy to be
back at the White House?"

00:00:59.125 --> 00:01:00.960
[ Laughter ]

00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:02.495
Actually,
to prove that he's fine,

00:01:02.495 --> 00:01:04.497
when Biden returned
to the White House last night,

00:01:04.497 --> 00:01:07.800
he jogged a couple steps
on the South lawn.

00:01:07.800 --> 00:01:14.040
I -- I think it helped.
Let's see how he did.

00:01:14.040 --> 00:01:16.509
-Yeah.
[ Cheers ]

00:01:16.509 --> 00:01:18.244
That's right.
That's right.

00:01:18.244 --> 00:01:23.282
That's right.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:23.282 --> 00:01:25.652
I'm sure that'll squash
all the conspiracy theories.

00:01:25.652 --> 00:01:27.386
[ Laughter ]

00:01:27.386 --> 00:01:28.921
It looked like he was gonna
try to catch a bus

00:01:28.921 --> 00:01:30.490
and then thought, "Ah, you know,
I'll wait for the next one."

00:01:30.490 --> 00:01:32.091
[ Laughter ]

00:01:32.091 --> 00:01:34.294
Some news from overseas.
Well, here's something

00:01:34.294 --> 00:01:35.662
I didn't expect
to be talking about.

00:01:35.662 --> 00:01:38.364
A massive cargo ship
got spun around

00:01:38.364 --> 00:01:42.402
and stuck in the Suez Canal,
blocking more than 100 ships.

00:01:42.402 --> 00:01:43.769
Look at this thing.
It's giant.

00:01:43.769 --> 00:01:45.604
Look at that.
[ Laughs ]

00:01:45.604 --> 00:01:47.774
If you look closely, the ship
has a tiny bumper sticker

00:01:47.774 --> 00:01:49.609
that says "Student driver."
So, I mean...

00:01:49.609 --> 00:01:51.945
-Oh, come on.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:51.945 --> 00:01:53.245
-Traffic is backed up for miles,

00:01:53.245 --> 00:01:54.814
and hundreds of ships
are delayed.

00:01:54.814 --> 00:01:56.449
Do you know how stressful it is
to parallel park

00:01:56.449 --> 00:01:57.984
when there's someone behind you?

00:01:57.984 --> 00:01:59.785
Imagine blocking
a whole hemisphere.

00:01:59.785 --> 00:02:02.321
You know what I'm saying?
[ Laughter ]

00:02:02.321 --> 00:02:03.656
Yeah, that's a tough day
for that captain.

00:02:03.656 --> 00:02:05.858
Right now, he's trending
worldwide on Twitter

00:02:05.858 --> 00:02:11.464
as #DockBlocker.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:11.464 --> 00:02:13.633
Listen to this --
I read that Pfizer has begun

00:02:13.633 --> 00:02:17.236
testing an oral anti-viral drug
for COVID.

00:02:17.236 --> 00:02:19.105
Man, if they can just
put the medicine

00:02:19.105 --> 00:02:20.573
into a chicken sandwich,

00:02:20.573 --> 00:02:22.942
America will flatten
the curve by Friday.

00:02:22.942 --> 00:02:25.545
[ Cheers and applause ]
By Friday!

00:02:25.545 --> 00:02:28.113
Trust me!

00:02:28.113 --> 00:02:30.616
Imagine if this oral drug
has to be refrigerated.

00:02:30.616 --> 00:02:31.951
Pfizer's gonna be like,

00:02:31.951 --> 00:02:34.387
"Have fun swallowing
a minus-80-degree ice marble."

00:02:34.387 --> 00:02:36.455
[ Laughter ]

00:02:36.455 --> 00:02:39.725
Meanwhile, researchers in Mexico
have invented a new mask.

00:02:39.725 --> 00:02:41.026
Higgins, you'll be very excited
about this.

00:02:41.026 --> 00:02:42.829
-I can't wait to hear about it.
-Now look at this.

00:02:42.829 --> 00:02:44.897
They invented a new mask
over in Mexico.

00:02:44.897 --> 00:02:47.900
They claim it reduces
the risk of infection

00:02:47.900 --> 00:02:49.002
while eating or talking.

00:02:49.002 --> 00:02:51.604
-Oh.
-Take a look at this.

00:02:51.604 --> 00:02:52.672
-There you go.

00:02:52.672 --> 00:02:57.243
[ Laughter ]

00:02:57.243 --> 00:02:59.178
-What?
-What?

00:02:59.178 --> 00:03:00.312
-What are you talking about?
-Dog nose?

00:03:00.312 --> 00:03:02.414
-What are you
talking about, man?

00:03:02.414 --> 00:03:04.049
That's it, right there.
That solves it.

00:03:04.049 --> 00:03:06.218
-It makes sense.
-It's got to reduce the risk

00:03:06.218 --> 00:03:08.621
by at least 50%.
-Yeah.

00:03:08.621 --> 00:03:10.957
Sure, man.
-Sure. Absolutely.

00:03:10.957 --> 00:03:13.792
[ Laughter ]

00:03:13.792 --> 00:03:15.595
I have a feeling
whatever's going that way

00:03:15.595 --> 00:03:17.563
is probably coming this way,
as well.

00:03:17.563 --> 00:03:18.631
But whatever.

00:03:18.631 --> 00:03:20.867
I mean, it looks like
a nose thong.

00:03:20.867 --> 00:03:22.101
[ Laughter ]

00:03:22.101 --> 00:03:24.170
-Nose diaper.
-The most interesting part is,

00:03:24.170 --> 00:03:28.140
underneath that is two even
tinier masks over each nostril.

00:03:28.140 --> 00:03:30.510
-Wow!
[ Laughter ]

00:03:30.510 --> 00:03:32.812
-Right now, the CDC
is calling it groundbreaking

00:03:32.812 --> 00:03:35.915
and wildly ineffective.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:35.915 --> 00:03:38.684
Some business news.
I saw that Southwest Airlines

00:03:38.684 --> 00:03:41.153
is doing away
with social distancing.

00:03:41.153 --> 00:03:43.022
It has decided to return

00:03:43.022 --> 00:03:45.358
to its pre-pandemic
boarding procedures.

00:03:45.358 --> 00:03:47.993
-Ooh.
-I think the real story here is

00:03:47.993 --> 00:03:51.030
that Southwest is claiming that
they have boarding procedures.

00:03:51.030 --> 00:03:53.165
[ Laughter ]

00:03:53.165 --> 00:03:54.767
If you don't remember
Southwest's old

00:03:54.767 --> 00:03:57.303
boarding procedure,
it's basically this.

00:03:57.303 --> 00:03:59.438
-And here we go!
-There you go. See?

00:03:59.438 --> 00:04:01.908
"Oh, I'm in section --
No --"

00:04:01.908 --> 00:04:05.244
[ Applause ]

00:04:05.244 --> 00:04:07.613
"Now seating the D section."
"No, I'm D!"

00:04:07.613 --> 00:04:10.950
"No, I'm sorry,
A first, then D."

00:04:10.950 --> 00:04:13.186
Speaking of air travel,
we mentioned this last month.

00:04:13.186 --> 00:04:14.821
We got thousands of letters.

00:04:14.821 --> 00:04:16.188
[ Chuckles ]
Did we?

00:04:16.188 --> 00:04:17.790
[ Laughter ]
-Why not? Why not?

00:04:17.790 --> 00:04:20.059
-I don't believe that.
But we got thousands of letters.

00:04:20.059 --> 00:04:21.894
-Thousands, man.
-People still write letters.

00:04:21.894 --> 00:04:23.028
-We got hundred and thousands
of letters.

00:04:23.028 --> 00:04:24.597
-That's correct.
We got thousands of letters

00:04:24.597 --> 00:04:25.965
asking us to talk about it
again, apparently.

00:04:25.965 --> 00:04:27.900
-Oh, good, good.
-Because the Philadelphia

00:04:27.900 --> 00:04:30.336
airport has a robot.
Do you remember this?

00:04:30.336 --> 00:04:32.839
-Yeah.
-It delivers food to travelers.

00:04:32.839 --> 00:04:35.107
But actually, the way
it works is, it's a robot,

00:04:35.107 --> 00:04:37.009
and then someone
who works there,

00:04:37.009 --> 00:04:40.112
and the robot follows
the person who works there.

00:04:40.112 --> 00:04:43.015
And then, that person --
the robot follows them,

00:04:43.015 --> 00:04:45.484
then, whoever's eating the food
has to go in the robot

00:04:45.484 --> 00:04:47.820
and get their sandwich,
at the robot.

00:04:47.820 --> 00:04:49.689
-That sounds efficient.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:49.689 --> 00:04:51.457
-Or they could just have
the human bring the sandwich

00:04:51.457 --> 00:04:53.626
over to the people.
Yeah, this much.

00:04:53.626 --> 00:04:55.661
-You don't want hands
on your hoagie.

00:04:55.661 --> 00:04:57.763
So, you know, the robot --
-Hey, don't talk dirty!

00:04:57.763 --> 00:04:59.298
[ Laughter ]
-No, he didn't mean that.

00:04:59.298 --> 00:05:00.532
No, no.
-What happened?

00:05:00.532 --> 00:05:02.234
I left,
and now it's a filth show?

00:05:02.234 --> 00:05:04.537
-No, in Philadelphia,
that means a sandwich.

00:05:04.537 --> 00:05:07.606
-Yeah. You don't want hands
on your hero.

00:05:07.606 --> 00:05:08.974
-Yeah, you know what?
-Hey!

00:05:08.974 --> 00:05:10.876
-Hey, Higgins.
No, hey.

00:05:10.876 --> 00:05:12.077
-Filthy!
-Yeah, no, no,

00:05:12.077 --> 00:05:13.212
he doesn't mean
that type of hero.

00:05:13.212 --> 00:05:15.248
He means a sandwich.
-Oh, okay.

00:05:15.248 --> 00:05:18.084
-It keeps paws off your po' boy.

00:05:18.084 --> 00:05:19.318
[ Laughter ]

00:05:19.318 --> 00:05:21.420
-Okay.
All right.

00:05:21.420 --> 00:05:24.690
-It's all getting --
-I've had enough of innuendos.

00:05:24.690 --> 00:05:26.258
-How does your sandwich
get made?

00:05:26.258 --> 00:05:27.660
How does your sandwich
get made?

00:05:27.660 --> 00:05:30.796
-I mean, safely, you know,
in a facility by other robots.

00:05:30.796 --> 00:05:32.331
-We can't just --

00:05:32.331 --> 00:05:34.066
[ Laughter ]

00:05:34.066 --> 00:05:35.401
Can't you just
get your sandwich there,

00:05:35.401 --> 00:05:37.270
and you handle it,
your sandwich?

00:05:37.270 --> 00:05:38.904
-I think, you know, they're
trying to cut down risk, man.

00:05:38.904 --> 00:05:41.540
Come on.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:41.540 --> 00:05:46.045
We do what we can, man.
-Or you do too much.

00:05:46.045 --> 00:05:48.348
[ Laughter ]

00:05:48.348 --> 00:05:50.316
Anyways, it delivers food
to travelers.

00:05:50.316 --> 00:05:51.650
But now, get this.

00:05:51.650 --> 00:05:53.953
This is what the Philadelphia
airport is doing now.

00:05:53.953 --> 00:05:56.188
They're asking
for name suggestions...

00:05:56.188 --> 00:05:57.356
-Oh, no.
-...for the robot.

00:05:57.356 --> 00:05:58.657
Just watch this.
-Ah.

00:05:58.657 --> 00:06:00.126
-The food delivery robot...
-That's the thing.

00:06:00.126 --> 00:06:01.527
-...at Philadelphia
International Airport

00:06:01.527 --> 00:06:03.963
needs a name, and the airport
wants your help.

00:06:03.963 --> 00:06:06.031
Travelers can come up
with a list of names,

00:06:06.031 --> 00:06:07.867
and the airport
will narrow them down.

00:06:07.867 --> 00:06:10.669
There will then be a contest
to pick the name.

00:06:10.669 --> 00:06:11.738
-This is such a bad idea.

00:06:11.738 --> 00:06:13.572
You're gonna let Philly
choose the name?

00:06:13.572 --> 00:06:14.806
-Yes!
-Perfect.

00:06:14.806 --> 00:06:15.808
Well, congratulations.

00:06:15.808 --> 00:06:17.676
Say hello to R2-D-Bag,
everybody.

00:06:17.676 --> 00:06:19.578
[ Laughter ]
You win! No, you win!

00:06:19.578 --> 00:06:21.214
You're right.
You're right.

00:06:21.214 --> 00:06:23.315
Let them choose.

00:06:23.315 --> 00:06:25.751
The robot's working now,
but next month, a Phillies fan

00:06:25.751 --> 00:06:27.753
will hurl that thing
at a Mets outfielder.

00:06:27.753 --> 00:06:28.855
Just trust me.
Watch.

00:06:28.855 --> 00:06:30.389
[ Laughter ]

00:06:30.389 --> 00:06:31.924
[ Grunts ]
-Boo!

00:06:31.924 --> 00:06:34.427
-Yeah, exactly.
Uh, listen to this.

00:06:34.427 --> 00:06:37.997
Wedding retailer David's Bridal.
You guys know David's Bridal?

00:06:37.997 --> 00:06:39.866
Well, they're saying that
weddings are coming back,

00:06:39.866 --> 00:06:42.601
but they're taking on
a more casual tone.

00:06:42.601 --> 00:06:44.102
Yeah.
It was only a matter of time

00:06:44.102 --> 00:06:47.272
before people were like, "Wait.
Is spending 5 grand on a dress

00:06:47.272 --> 00:06:50.943
you only wear once stupid?"
[ Laughter ]

00:06:50.943 --> 00:06:53.045
"It is?"
[ Laughter ]

00:06:53.045 --> 00:06:54.914
It's getting so casual,
David's Bridal is keeping

00:06:54.914 --> 00:06:57.483
all their dresses in bins
like it's T.J.Maxx.

00:06:57.483 --> 00:06:59.652
[ Laughter ]

00:06:59.652 --> 00:07:01.186
"You looking for a dress?
Yeah, no problem.

00:07:01.186 --> 00:07:04.156
We have -- this whole bin
is small to extra large."

00:07:04.156 --> 00:07:05.892
[ Laughter ]

00:07:05.892 --> 00:07:09.061
"We don't put it in size.
It's just in that pile."

00:07:09.061 --> 00:07:10.896
Well, now, guys, everyone
is keeping a close eye

00:07:10.896 --> 00:07:13.765
on their brackets ahead of
next week's Final Four,

00:07:13.765 --> 00:07:15.000
but we thought it'd be fun
to pick a different kind

00:07:15.000 --> 00:07:16.369
of Final Four.
That's right.

00:07:16.369 --> 00:07:18.871
It's time for
a "News Flub Final Four."

00:07:18.871 --> 00:07:20.005
Here we go.

00:07:20.005 --> 00:07:21.507
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:21.507 --> 00:07:25.111
♪♪

00:07:25.111 --> 00:07:27.846
-Okay.
Let's look at our picks here.

00:07:27.846 --> 00:07:31.083
Oh, there they are.
Our top four news flubs.

00:07:31.083 --> 00:07:32.919
First, we have a reporter

00:07:32.919 --> 00:07:35.287
who runs into some issues
with her microphone.

00:07:35.287 --> 00:07:37.089
Let's see how it goes.

00:07:37.089 --> 00:07:38.623
-Annette Lawless
is live on the scene,

00:07:38.623 --> 00:07:42.528
tracking down new information.
Good morning, Annette.

00:07:42.528 --> 00:07:43.696
[ Low, robotic voice ]
That's right, Gloria.

00:07:43.696 --> 00:07:46.699
Those fire crews
are still out here right now.

00:07:46.699 --> 00:07:50.936
[ Laughter, cheers, applause ]

00:07:50.936 --> 00:07:52.871
-It's the Philly robot.
Yeah.

00:07:52.871 --> 00:07:54.740
-No, yeah.
I watch her all --

00:07:54.740 --> 00:07:57.743
She's on SNN,
Satanic News Network.

00:07:57.743 --> 00:07:59.612
Yeah, I've seen her before.
[ Laughter ]

00:07:59.612 --> 00:08:01.580
"Honey, you have a great voice
for broadcasting."

00:08:01.580 --> 00:08:02.748
-"Thank you."
-"Thank you."

00:08:02.748 --> 00:08:07.253
[ Laughter ]

00:08:07.253 --> 00:08:09.388
"The followers of Satan
thank you."

00:08:09.388 --> 00:08:11.223
[ Laughter ]

00:08:11.223 --> 00:08:12.758
Let's get back
to the board here.

00:08:12.758 --> 00:08:14.961
This next clip,
a news anchor in Virginia

00:08:14.961 --> 00:08:17.396
realizes he's made
an unfortunate mistake.

00:08:17.396 --> 00:08:19.331
Take a look at this.

00:08:19.331 --> 00:08:23.869
-Check you're the panties.
About 175,000 rice --

00:08:23.869 --> 00:08:25.805
I think that was
supposed to be "pantries."

00:08:25.805 --> 00:08:28.808
[ Laughter ]

00:08:28.808 --> 00:08:31.610
-I couldn't warn you
before I saw it.

00:08:31.610 --> 00:08:34.780
[ Laughter ]
-"Check your panties!"

00:08:34.780 --> 00:08:39.151
[ Laughter ]

00:08:39.151 --> 00:08:41.386
-Rice.
[ Laughter ]

00:08:41.386 --> 00:08:44.623
-Let's look
at another clip here.

00:08:44.623 --> 00:08:46.759
This next one is a BBC anchor,

00:08:46.759 --> 00:08:49.161
and he's about to start
the news broadcast.

00:08:49.161 --> 00:08:51.263
But, man, he struggles
to find his spot.

00:08:51.263 --> 00:08:53.098
Take a look at this.

00:08:53.098 --> 00:08:57.002
♪♪

00:08:57.002 --> 00:08:59.572
-Oh.
[ Laughter ]

00:09:05.978 --> 00:09:07.312
-Yeah.

00:09:07.312 --> 00:09:08.714
No.

00:09:08.714 --> 00:09:10.182
[ Laughter ]

00:09:10.182 --> 00:09:11.550
-Hello, and welcome.

00:09:11.550 --> 00:09:13.351
-Yeah!
[ Applause ]

00:09:13.351 --> 00:09:15.020
Stuck the landing.
-Nailed it.

00:09:15.020 --> 00:09:17.723
-Stuck the landing.
[ Laughter ]

00:09:17.723 --> 00:09:21.660
"What?
All right. What?"

00:09:21.660 --> 00:09:24.062
[ Laughter ]

00:09:24.062 --> 00:09:27.166
"Hello, and welcome."
It's like...

00:09:27.166 --> 00:09:29.267
Well, here's our
last pick here.

00:09:29.267 --> 00:09:32.371
This clip is about a man
who had some trouble with Zoom.

00:09:32.371 --> 00:09:34.706
I'm sure you saw it.
Take a look at this.

00:09:34.706 --> 00:09:37.710
-A Texas lawyer proves
that technical difficulties

00:09:37.710 --> 00:09:40.045
can happen
even at the worst of times.

00:09:40.045 --> 00:09:42.581
-Can you hear me, Judge?
-I can hear you.

00:09:42.581 --> 00:09:44.382
I think it's a filter.

00:09:44.382 --> 00:09:46.885
-I'm here live.
I'm not a cat.

00:09:46.885 --> 00:09:49.788
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:09:49.788 --> 00:09:51.023
-All right, what do you think?

00:09:51.023 --> 00:09:53.125
Was it the reporter
with audio issues?

00:09:53.125 --> 00:09:55.461
-Yeah.
-Was it, "Check your pantries"?

00:09:55.461 --> 00:09:59.331
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:09:59.331 --> 00:10:02.034
Was it confused BBC?

00:10:02.034 --> 00:10:03.235
[ Light applause ]

00:10:03.235 --> 00:10:05.470
You don't have to boo him.
[ Laughter ]

00:10:05.470 --> 00:10:08.574
The guy had a rough day already.
Gosh, now you're booing him.

00:10:08.574 --> 00:10:10.542
Or cat lawyer?

00:10:10.542 --> 00:10:12.177
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:10:12.177 --> 00:10:13.311
I think it's
"Check your pantries."

00:10:13.311 --> 00:10:15.080
-Yeah!
-"Check your pantries!"

00:10:15.080 --> 00:10:16.081
We have a winner!

00:10:16.081 --> 00:10:17.916
♪♪

00:10:17.916 --> 00:10:20.920
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:10:20.920 --> 00:10:23.689
Some entertainment news.
This summer, Disney is releasing

00:10:23.689 --> 00:10:29.661
"Black Widow" and "Cruella"
on Disney+ $29.99 each, yeah.

00:10:29.661 --> 00:10:31.897
When you drop 30 bucks
to watch a movie at home,

00:10:31.897 --> 00:10:34.934
Disney+ just starts playing
a clip of Jafar laughing.

00:10:34.934 --> 00:10:36.902
[ Laughter ]

00:10:36.902 --> 00:10:38.270
And, finally,
this is pretty strange.

00:10:38.270 --> 00:10:40.706
Here in New York,
this week, dolphins were spotted

00:10:40.706 --> 00:10:42.608
swimming in the East River.

00:10:42.608 --> 00:10:44.843
Check this out.
It's real.

00:10:44.843 --> 00:10:48.914
-Look at that.

00:10:48.914 --> 00:10:51.650
Wow.
Yeah, amazing.

00:10:51.650 --> 00:10:53.619
They're the only dolphins
that smoke cigarettes

00:10:53.619 --> 00:10:55.087
through their blowholes.
-Wow.

00:10:55.087 --> 00:11:00.025
[ Laughter and applause ]
-Unbelievable.

00:11:00.025 --> 00:11:01.493
After a few hours
in the East River,

00:11:01.493 --> 00:11:02.795
they became
the first marine life

00:11:02.795 --> 00:11:04.497
to check themselves
into Sea World.

00:11:04.497 --> 00:11:08.733
[ Laughter ]

00:11:08.733 --> 00:11:11.036
-Oh!
-I got to be honest,

00:11:11.036 --> 00:11:13.471
it's nice to hear about sea life
unexpectedly showing up

00:11:13.471 --> 00:11:15.741
in something other than
Cinnamon Toast Crunch.

